{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE FOR THE TWO UNMET CLOSE CRITERIA. The first is a case where the ACCEPTANCE CRITERION\nANTICIPATED A DIFFERENT (AND WORSE) FIX SHAPE than the one implemented; the second is genuinely\noutstanding and in flight.\n\n=== CRITERION 1: 'cells 2 and 4 invert'. CELL 4 DID INVERT. CELL 2 MUST NOT, AND THAT IS THE FIX\nWORKING AS DESIGNED — NOT AN OMISSION. ===\n\nCell 2 is test_the_mint_is_a_no_op_on_the_shape_the_update_path_hands_it, and it still asserts\n    rebar.resolve_mapping('jira', _DC_USER, repo_root=store) is None\ni.e. that _ensure_inbound_assignee_identity STILL mints nothing when handed a BARE STRING.\n\nTHAT ASSERTION IS CORRECT AFTER THE FIX, because the fix does not change what the mint accepts — it\nchanges WHAT THE CALLER HANDS IT. The mint's dict guard at _ensure_inbound_assignee_identity:105-106\n('if not isinstance(assignee, dict): return') is DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. The defect was never that\nthe guard existed; it was that inbound_differ dropped the canonical  the mapper\nhad already computed, so the applier had only the scalar to pass. The fix restores the identity at\nthe source: the differ now forwards , and the applier keys on\n.\n\nINVERTING CELL 2 WOULD REQUIRE MAKING THE MINT ACCEPT A BARE STRING — WHICH IS THE ONE FIX THAT WAS\nEXPLICITLY PROHIBITED, and for a concrete reason. On Data Center the scalar happens to be \n(== the external id), so a string-accepting mint LOOKS correct there. On CLOUD the scalar is the\nDISPLAY NAME, so minting keyed on it would register every Cloud user under the wrong id — turning a\nsilent no-op into silent DATA CORRUPTION, which is strictly worse than the bug being fixed. That is\nwhy the prohibition was a hard constraint on this work and why cell 2 keeps its polarity: it is now\nthe REGRESSION GUARD against that wrong fix, pinned by a test instead of holding by accident.\n\nCELL 4 DID INVERT, as the criterion expects: test_the_mapper_already_carries_everything_the_mint_needs\npreviously pinned '\"assignee_identity\" not in changed' as the defect's mechanism, and now asserts\nthe forwarded value equals the mapper's own canonical identity. Its intent is preserved and the\nreason is recorded in its docstring.\n\nTHE CLOUD GUARD IS THE INDEPENDENT PROOF THAT THE CHOSEN SHAPE IS THE RIGHT ONE:\ntest_the_cloud_update_path_keys_on_the_account_id_not_the_display_name drives the real differ and the\nreal applier phase with {accountId: 5b10a2844c20165700ede21g, displayName: 'Ada Lovelace'} and\nasserts the mint registers under the ACCOUNT ID and that resolve_mapping('jira', 'Ada Lovelace') is\nNone. A string-accepting fix passes on DC and FAILS that cell. So the two cells together encode the\ndistinction the criterion was reaching for.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE that both boundaries are independently pinned (so nothing is passing vacuously):\nreverting the differ's forwarding -> 4 failed / 3 passed; reverting ONLY the applier's keying -> 2\nfailed / 5 passed WITH THE DIFFER CELL STILL GREEN. All AssertionError, no AttributeError/ImportError.\n\n=== CRITERION 2: the J11 live cell. GENUINELY OUTSTANDING, RUN IN FLIGHT. ===\ntest_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity needs a harness run on a tree containing this\nfix, with NO weakening of its assertions. Status:\n * the fix merged as ff7a761267 (Gerrit 1232), and its RED-first companion as c83263b7d4 (1231);\n * harness run **30772461871** was dispatched against main @ bd3de0f864, which contains both;\n * the oracle itself is UNCHANGED by this ticket — it is exactly as it landed in 1226/1227, so a\n   green there cannot come from a relaxed assertion. That is the point: the cell was failing because\n   the PRODUCT was wrong, and this ticket fixed the product.\nThe previous run (30767546938, main @ d72c4777d3, pre-fix) failed that cell with 'THE PASS MINTED\nNOTHING', so the pair of runs will be a controlled before/after rather than a bare green.\nDO NOT close this ticket until that run reports the cell PASSED — and read the per-cell verdict plus\nthe '[jira-live-canary] collected=N executed=N skipped=0' line, not the pass/fail count."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785714256591496001,"uuid":"520c6d12-c133-4daf-8290-9dcbacd67625"}